<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lycortas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Lycortas of Megalopolis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lycortas of Megalopolis was a statesman and general of the Achaean League in the early 2nd century BCE and the father of the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>. A close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philopoemen">Philopoemen</a>, he led the league after Philopoemen was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messenians">Messenians</a>, recovering Messene in 182 BCE. He defended the league's independence against growing Roman interference in its affairs.</p></div>
